  "id": "dva",
  "name": "D.Va",
  "role": "Bruiser",
  "overview": "D.Va is a Bruiser who combines unique utility with reliable damage mitigation together with a solid damage output and a high amount of survivability when played at her maximum potential.",
  "strengths": [
    "Good survivability",
    "Decent mobility",
    "Reliable damage mitigation",
    "Good at capturing Mercenary Camps",
    "Powerful zoning potential"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Susceptible to area of effect crowd control on the ground stopping Boosters",
    "Predictable spawn position for D.Va's Pilot when her Mech gets destroyed by damage",
    "Lack of Mount while in Mech Mode, however, Boosters helps with that"
  ],
  "synergies": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "garrosh",
        "name": "Garrosh"
      },
      {
        "id": "maiev",
        "name": "Maiev"
      },
      {
        "id": "falstad",
        "name": "Falstad"
      },
      {
        "id": "deckard",
        "name": "Deckard Cain"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "D.Va is good when paired with Heroes that can play around her powerful Self-Destruct by displacing or locking enemy Heroes within its range with crowd control effects (for example Deckard Cain with Stay Awhile and Listen and/or Scroll Of Sealing) or by moving the exploding Mech (such as Into the Fray by Garrosh).\n\nBoosters are useful to combo with unique Heroes that require an allied Hero to move fast (for example Anduin with Lightbomb) or that can benefit from enemy Heroes being knocked away at the right moment (such as Maiev using Umbral Bind)."
  },
  "counters": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "e-t-c",
        "name": "E.T.C."
      },
      {
        "id": "malthael",
        "name": "Malthael"
      },
      {
        "id": "raynor",
        "name": "Raynor"
      },
      {
        "id": "kaelthas",
        "name": "Kael'thas"
      },
      {
        "id": "stukov",
        "name": "Stukov"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Like many Heroes in the game, D.Va suffers against crowd control paired with burst damage as they can drastically reduce the value she can get from Mech Mode by bursting her down before she can use Self-Destruct to restore the Health of her Mech.\n\nAs she spawns in a predictable position when her Mech dies, it is also easy to throw Abilities in that area to hit her (such as Entangling Roots by Malfurion). Similarly, a well-timed interrupt while she is channeling Call Mech is a powerful tool to take her down.\n\nWhile solo laning, D.Va has a hard time against Heroes who can easily outtrade her in a duel on Maps where there is a Capture Point to contest (such as Braxis Holdout) or that can rotate faster than her while double soaking on other Maps."
  },
