    "explanation": "D.Va tends to perform best on small to medium-sized Maps with lots of narrow choke points where she can get value from Self-Destruct for zoning away enemy Heroes (for example Infernal Shrines).\n\nAs Self-Destruct will get Charge progress based on how much time D.Va spends Basic Attacking with her Mech, she prefers playing on Maps where double soak is possible because that way she can Basic Attack enemy Minions twice as often compared to when staying in a single lane.\n\nDue to her lack of Mount while in Mech Mode, she does not like big Maps that much (such as Warhead Junction)."
  },
  "builds": [
    {
      "name": "Defense Matrix Build",
      "label": "Recommended",
      "description": "D.Va's Defense Matrix Build primarily focuses on reducing the damage done and the healing received by enemy Heroes, provided that the enemy team lets you channel Defense Matrix most of the time.\n\nThe area increase from Diverting Power at Level 16 is great for peeling for your teammates. The healing reduction from Aggression Matrix at Level 4 and the Armor reduction from Target Locked at Level 13 help to secure kills.\n\nWhen playing this Build, you should ideally use Defense Matrix on enemy Heroes who are dealing damage to yourself or to your teammates and on enemy Heroes who are being attacked by your teammates.",
